      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/Blue-B/pi-custom-packages\n\n### Category\n\nJS\n\n### Project Title\n\nTen extensions for the pi terminal coding agent\n\n### Project Description\n\nA monorepo of ten TypeScript extensions for pi, a terminal AI coding agent. It fixes long-session failures (bash timeout unit, stale model identity, image bloat) and lets an agent running in WSL capture, click, and record the Windows desktop.\n\n### Highlights\n\nMost extension packs for coding agents add features. Half of these remove failure modes that only show up after hours in one session: a model passing milliseconds to a timeout measured in seconds, a model naming the previous model after you switch, twenty screenshots re-sent on every turn.\n\nThe Windows side is the unusual part. pi runs inside WSL and cannot see the desktop hosting it, so these drive it over WSL interop with plain PowerShell, no extra Linux dependency. Window capture uses PrintWindow, so a window buried under five others still comes out clean, and sensitive regions can be masked before the image reaches the model.\n\nThe repo also shrank on purpose. Six packages were deleted, three of them because pi absorbed the feature upstream. One of those upstream fixes started from an issue the author filed (earendil-works/pi#5369, fixed in #7330).\n\n### Example Code\n\n```bash\npi install git:github.com/Blue-B/pi-custom-packages\n```\n",
